import STFSpec.Hash

/-!
# Packed Keccak primary and representation guards

Library `EthConformance`. Six published selected KAT facts come from
https://keccak.team/obsolete/KeccakKAT-3.zip, archive SHA-256
`af92d22d23527a0d168a6bbe70b28c840a43bba5bcea828a6d9a5e7ad79378ce`.
Zero permutation: `KeccakKAT/KeccakPermutationIntermediateValues.txt`, first
all-zero example, State after permutation, member SHA-256
`db0947545a5d91c20b2105aac75fac430deafe0ccaecb660af60044244df30d4`.
Keccak-256: `KeccakKAT/ShortMsgKAT_256.txt`, Len=0/1080/1088/1096, member SHA-256
`741862f92342010311504202d7b304955fa28aa03a752633a5e83f971f014851`.
Keccak-512: `KeccakKAT/ShortMsgKAT_512.txt`, Len=0, member SHA-256
`04164af3d89aa847b0dfe02d9c0be10c42fd72cdcdad0228566dac6143690a46`.
All expected values are selected primary facts, not host-computed constants.
Additional bounded guards cover coordinates, simultaneous chi and sponge seams.
Spec guidance: `STFSpec/informal/modules/EthHash.md` §§3–4,7.
-/

